cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use vibe-forge or its benchmark data in your research, please cite it as follows."
authors:
  - family-names: "Bhaskar"
    given-names: "Mayank"
title: "vibe-forge: local-first policy router for coding assistants"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-16"
url: "https://github.com/qtjg/vibe-forge"
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - "llm-routing"
  - "ollama"
  - "local-first"
  - "benchmarking"
  - "code-assistants"
abstract: >-
  vibe-forge routes coding subtasks to different local LLMs served by Ollama
  based on task complexity, keeping every inference on-device. It ships a
  deterministic heuristic scorer with explainable decisions, a
  cheapest-covering-model tier registry, a fixed 36-task benchmark suite that
  emits pandas-friendly CSV results, and a live dashboard.
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Ollama"
    notes: "Local LLM server used for all inference."
    url: "https://ollama.com"